Hello, our name is Customertimes , but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.
Project description:
You build and own the user-facing application: fast, usable by everyone, installable, and reliable, including offline scenarios.
Location: India (Remote)
How you'll make an impact :

• Develop and maintain the web client using React 19, TypeScript, and Vite;

• Implement Progressive Web App features: service workers, caching strategies, offline support, installability, and push notifications where relevant;

• Consume GraphQL APIs efficiently (e.g., Apollo Client or urql), with sound state and cache management;

• Build a reusable, WCAG-compliant component library and maintain design consistency;

• Optimize performance (bundle size, Core Web Vitals, rendering behavior);

• Write unit, component, and end-to-end tests; collaborate with QA on automation;

• Participate in code reviews and mentor less experienced engineers;

• Collaborate with the Solution Architect, backend engineers, and designers on technical approach.

What makes you a great fit :

• 5+ years of frontend development, with strong production experience in React and TypeScript;

• Hands-on experience with Vite and modern build tooling;

• Practical PWA experience (service workers, Workbox, manifest, offline strategies);

• Experience with GraphQL clients and client-side state management;

• Strong grasp of HTML/CSS, responsive design, and WCAG compliance;

• Experience with testing tools (Vitest/Jest, React Testing Library, Playwright/Cypress);

• Familiarity with Git workflows and CI pipelines.

You are a star if you have :

• Experience with React 19 features (Actions, use, Server Components concepts, the React Compiler);

• Data visualization experience;

• Frontend security and performance monitoring experience.

If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community - Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?
